      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic structured document extraction task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nImplement the initial file extract_invoice_fields.py using Microsoft/OpenAI.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] extract_invoice_fields.py - extracts vendor, date, total, and line-item fields from an invoice\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] extract_receipt_fields.py - extracts merchant, tax, total, and items from a receipt\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] normalize_expense.py - normalizes extracted expense fields into a standard JSON schema\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] validate_document_fields.py - validates required structured fields and confidence scores\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] document_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Structured Document Extraction\n6. [HELPER] document_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Structured Document Extraction\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] invoice_summary.py - Summarize extracted invoice fields\n8. [LATER-STEP] vendor_text_safety.py - Moderate vendor notes or memo fields\n9. [LATER-STEP] invoice_note_translate.py - Translate extracted invoice notes or descriptions\n10. [LATER-STEP] expense_record_store.py - Persist normalized expense records in a managed document store\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
